  "Number": 12,
  "Question": "Antonette gets \\(70 \\%\\) on a \\(10\\)-problem test, \\(80 \\%\\) on a \\(20\\)-problem test and \\(90 \\%\\) on a \\(30\\)-problem test. If the three tests are combined into one \\(60\\)-problem test, which percent is closest to her overall score?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(40\\)",
    "B": "\\(77\\)",
    "C": "\\(80\\)",
    "D": "\\(83\\)",
    "E": "\\(87\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since the tests contain different numbers of problems, first find how many answers Antonette gets correct on each test:\n\\[\n0.70\\cdot10=7,\\qquad\n0.80\\cdot20=16,\\qquad\n0.90\\cdot30=27.\n\\]\nCombining the tests gives \\(7+16+27=50\\) correct answers out of \\(60\\) problems. Her overall percentage is\n\\[\n\\frac{50}{60}\\cdot100\\%=83\\frac13\\%.\n\\]\nThis rounds to \\(83\\%\\), which is among the choices and is the closest listed value. The answer is \\(83\\%\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
